@startuml admissions_shortlists_use_case

' ============================================================
' RecruitBook Standard PlantUML Style Configuration
' ============================================================

skinparam backgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam handwritten false
skinparam roundcorner 14
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam defaultFontColor #0F172A
skinparam dpi 160
skinparam padding 4
skinparam nodesep 55
skinparam ranksep 45

skinparam ArrowColor #334155
skinparam ArrowFontColor #0F172A
skinparam ArrowFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.2

skinparam TitleFontName Arial
skinparam TitleFontSize 22
skinparam TitleFontColor #020617
skinparam TitleFontStyle bold

skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FEF3C7
skinparam NoteBorderColor #B45309
skinparam NoteFontColor #78350F
skinparam NoteFontSize 13

skinparam actor {
  BackgroundColor #DBEAFE
  BorderColor #1D4ED8
  FontColor #0F172A
  FontStyle bold
}
skinparam usecase {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #2563EB
  FontColor #0F172A
}

title RecruitBook Batch 6 — Admissions Shortlists Use Case Slice

left to right direction

actor "Verified Admissions Officer\n(role=admissions_officer,\nstatus=verified)" as AdmissionsOfficer
actor "Platform\nAdministrator" as Admin

rectangle "Batch 6 — Admissions Shortlists" {
  usecase "Save a currently-visible\nstudent profile to private shortlist\n(ShortlistEntry.save)" as UC_Save
  usecase "List currently-visible\nsaved students\n(ShortlistEntry.listSaved)" as UC_List
  usecase "Remove own shortlist entry\n(ShortlistEntry.remove)" as UC_Remove

  usecase "Read shortlist entries\n(ShortlistEntry.readAllEntries —\nread-only, per the existing\nplatform-admin policy pattern)" as UC_AdminRead
}

AdmissionsOfficer --> UC_Save
AdmissionsOfficer --> UC_List
AdmissionsOfficer --> UC_Remove

Admin --> UC_AdminRead

note top of AdmissionsOfficer
  Every shortlist action requires a VERIFIED
  admissions officer. Pending or suspended
  admissions-officer accounts are blocked —
  not successful actors here.
end note

note right of UC_Save
  AccessPolicy gate (WITH CHECK):
  is_admissions_visible_profile(student_profile_id)
  must hold at insert time. A hidden or
  nonexistent profile id fails with the same
  fixed generic error. Saving an already-saved
  profile is idempotent — same generic success,
  no duplicate row, no oracle.
end note

note bottom of UC_List
  The saved list is a LIVE, re-gated view,
  not a static record. Each read re-checks
  is_admissions_visible_profile(student_profile_id)
  at query time. A now-hidden/withdrawn/
  suspended-owner entry disappears immediately
  with no distinct "stale" state or count; a
  later re-publish resurfaces it automatically.
  Rendered rows show only the same four approved
  discovery-summary fields as the existing
  discovery list (preferredName, country,
  cityRegion, intendedMajor) — never a full,
  unrestricted StudentProfile read.
end note

note bottom of UC_Remove
  AMENDED mechanism (post-Group-1a): removal is
  via the hardened SECURITY DEFINER RPC
  remove_own_admissions_shortlist_entry(uuid),
  NOT a direct DELETE policy (none exists; DELETE
  privilege is revoked from authenticated). The
  RPC bypasses RLS internally and re-implements
  ownership + verified-officer checks in its own
  WHERE clause, deliberately NOT visibility-gated,
  so a stale entry can still be removed. A foreign,
  stale, or nonexistent entry id is a silent no-op
  inside the RPC, returning the same generic
  result as removing a real entry — no distinction.
end note

note right of UC_AdminRead
  Follows the SAME platform-admin read-only
  POLICY PATTERN established for every prior
  table — NOT existing access, since this table
  does not exist yet (Group 1a charter, pending
  Group 2). Once built, admin access is read-only
  and not gated by admissions visibility; admin
  cannot save or remove entries.
end note

note as N_Excluded
  Deliberately NOT actors / NOT shown:
  * Student (zero shortlist visibility of any kind)
  * Counselor (zero shortlist access of any kind)
  * Pending/suspended admissions officer (verified gate fails)
  * Named or multiple shortlists; Shortlist.create(name)
  * Entry notes, labels, or tags
  * Search, filters, or ranking
  * Messaging, notifications, or exports
  * AI features or uploads
  * Audit events
  * Admissions writes to student_profiles,
    profile_visibility_settings, counselor_student_links,
    counselor_review_requests, or counselor_feedback_notes
end note

@enduml
